OBJECTS

FUNCTION

- Objects in JavaScript allow you to store key-value pairs, where each value can be referred to by its key. You can create a dictionary using curly braces \{ \}. The code below creates an object called cityData with some information about Johor.
- var cityData = \{
- 'city': 'Thimphu',
- 'coordinates': [83.63, 27.47],
- 'population': 114,551
- \};
- print(cityData);

- Functions take user inputs, use them to carry out some computation, and send an output back. Functions allow you to group a set of operations together and repeat the same operations with different parameters without having to rewrite them every time.
- var greet = function(name) \{    return 'Hello ' + name;\};print(greet('World'));print(greet('Readers'));

